# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: hosted-engine-first-request-stall: a hosted clautolisp engine sat at READY 0 for 30 s before picking up request 1
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-hosted-engine-first-request-stall
#+DATE: 2026-10-14

* Symptom

On 2026-10-14 (clautolisp / alfe 2.3.18, macOS arm64, SBCL),
=make -C autolisp-front-end test= failed one check out of 2265:

: PROTOCOL-FAILURE-INSIDE-A-LOADED-FILE-FAILS-THAT-REQUEST
:   a failure in a loaded file must fail ITS request, got "READY 0"

=drive-hosted-engine= (=autolisp-front-end/tests/file-protocol-tests.lisp=)
sends each form through stdin.txt and waits 30 s for =DONE n=. On a miss
it recorded only the current status. Here that status was still
=READY 0=, so the engine had not even published =RUNNING 1=
(=autolisp-protocol-server-loop= publishes it as soon as it reads a
request).

The engine did pick request 1 up later: =send-stdin= for request 2 waits
at most 5 s for the slot to be free and did not signal =:stdin-busy=,
and requests 2-4 all ended as expected. So request 1 was consumed
somewhere between 30 and 35 s after it was sent.

* Reproduction (not reproduced)

- The test on its own: 7/7 checks pass.
- The full suite rerun right afterwards on the same machine: 2265/2265
  pass, in 5m22 of wall-clock time. The failing run took 10m44 with about
  the same user time (4m31 vs 4m05), so that machine was probably loaded
  by something else.

* What was checked

- =autolisp-protocol-remote-read-line= polls stdin.txt every 100 ms
  (=autolisp-protocol-yield=, vlax-sleep). There is no back-off that
  could grow to 30 s.
- The host publishes stdin.txt by rename (=write-atomic-file=). The
  engine deletes the file only once it has read some lines from it.
  Neither side shows a race that could lose or hide the file.
- =READY 0= is published right before the loop starts, so no setup work
  runs between it and the first poll.

The leading hypothesis is a scheduling stall under load. A 30 s stall
before the first poll succeeds is still long enough to need explaining.

* Diagnostics added (clautolisp / alfe 2.3.19)

On a miss, =drive-hosted-engine= now records
: <current status> [miss: stdin-present=yes|no engine-alive=yes|no elapsed=N.Ns]
(=%hosted-engine-miss-record=). The status still comes first, so the
existing =" OK"= / =" FAIL"= checks read it unchanged. How to read the
next occurrence:

- =stdin-present=yes engine-alive=yes=: the engine is alive and has not
  polled. Look at scheduling, vlax-sleep and the heartbeat write.
- =stdin-present=no=, status still =READY 0=: the request was consumed
  and RUNNING was never published. Look at the read path and the status
  write.
- =engine-alive=no=: the engine died. Check =engine-stderr.txt= in the
  kept workdir.

* Next steps

1. Wait for a recurrence that carries the miss record.
2. If it shows a live engine that has not polled, measure the poll
   cadence under load (heartbeat.txt timestamps) before raising the
   30 s budget. Raising it would only hide the stall.
